      'Setup example: 0 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first player or partnership to reach the agreed target score (25 in original McLoughlin rules, or 40 in many editions) by winning tricks and scoring points from the Lost Heir card (+5) while avoiding the Wrong Boy penalty (-3); blank cards cancel the Heir or Wrong Boy when played to the same trick.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. **Bidding**: Players bid for the right to choose the Trump city. The bid is the number of tricks they expect to win (plus bonus cards). 2. **Special Cards**: The Lost Heir (highest trump, +5 points), The Wrong Boy (penalty card, -3 points), Blank City Cards (can negate points). 3. **Trick Play**: Must follow suit. If unable, play any card (including trump). Highest card of led suit wins, or highest trump. Each trick = 1 point.',
